msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:86
msgid "These eight notes are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:92
msgid "Send this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:93
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:94
msgid "``NOTE_C4*``, ``NOTE_D4*``, ``NOTE_E4*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:95
msgid "low C, D, E"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:96
msgid "``NOTE_F4*``, ``NOTE_G4*``, ``NOTE_A4*``, ``NOTE_B4*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:97
msgid "F, G, A, B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:98
msgid "``NOTE_C5*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:99
msgid "C one octave higher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:103
msgid "**Do not forget the star.** Without it the sketch keeps waiting for the end of the message, nothing is played and the Serial Monitor prints nothing either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:108
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:110
msgid "**The buzzer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:118
msgid "``tone(pin, frequency)`` starts a square wave at that frequency - a plain piezo buzzer then plays it. ``NOTE_C4`` is not a pin number but a frequency defined by the Arduino core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:122
msgid "**Collecting characters until the star**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:136
msgid "Characters are collected one by one. The star is both the trigger to act **and** the thing to remove: ``substring(0, length()-1)`` drops the last character, so ``NOTE_C4*`` becomes ``NOTE_C4``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:140
msgid "**Comparing text**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:147
msgid "Text is compared with the double-quote form and with ``==``. A single ``=`` would assign instead of compare and the code would compile but never work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:150
msgid "**Reset after every note**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/13-iot_Bluetooth_piano.rst:158
msgid "Clearing ``noteType`` is essential: without it the next note would be appended to the previous one and no comparison would ever match again."
msgstr ""
